      "text": "To find the value of the expression \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\), we can use the formula for the square of a binomial, which states that \\((a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\\). Here, we can rewrite the given expression in a form that matches this formula.\n\nThe given expression is:\n\\[23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\]\n\nWe can identify \\(a = 23\\) and \\(b = 2\\). Therefore, the expression can be rewritten as:\n\\[(23 + 2)^2\\]\n\nNow, we calculate the value inside the parentheses:\n\\[23 + 2 = 25\\]\n\nSo, the expression becomes:\n\\[25^2\\]\n\nNext, we compute \\(25^2\\):\n\\[25^2 = 25 \\times 25 = 625\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\) is \\(\\boxed{625}\\).",
