      "text": "We can recognize that the expression $23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2$ follows the form of a perfect square trinomial. The general form of a perfect square trinomial is $(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2$. In this case, $a = 23$ and $b = 2$.\n\nUsing the formula for the perfect square trinomial, we can rewrite the given expression as:\n\\[\n23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2 = (23 + 2)^2\n\\]\n\nNow, we simplify the expression inside the parentheses:\n\\[\n23 + 2 = 25\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n(23 + 2)^2 = 25^2\n\\]\n\nFinally, we calculate $25^2$:\n\\[\n25^2 = 625\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of $23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2$ is $\\boxed{625}$.",
